+kore-exec: [221605] Warning (WarnStuckClaimState):
+    The configuration's term unifies with the destination's term, but the
+    implication check between the conditions has failed.
+Context:
+  #Not ( { false #Equals bracketSpec ( -1 , ")" ) } )
+#And
+  <mpy>
+    <k> boolVal ( bracketSpec ( -1 , ")" ) ) ~> .K </k>
+    <functions> .Map </functions>
+    <env> .Map </env>
+  </mpy>
+[Error] Prover: backend terminated because the configuration cannot be
+rewritten further. See output for more details.
+exit=1
+
+This confirms the [total] declaration does not by itself assign a false result
+to the uncovered N < 0/non-"(" case.  It also confirms that the four candidate
+equations are not total over all Int x String, even though every value reachable
+from SPEC.loop's N >= 0 precondition is covered.

